<title>SWEDEN: TABLE - SKF posts lower H1 '97 profit.</title>
<headline>TABLE - SKF posts lower H1 '97 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bearings maker SKF reports its results for the six months ending June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>			 (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  1,103 vs  1,475</p>
<p> Sales					18,747 vs 17,528</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)		5.90  vs  7.90</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold		     13,839 vs 12,545</p>
<p> Selling and admin costs		 3,369 vs  3,309</p>
<p> Other op income/expense	  CREDIT  18 vs     17 CHARGE</p>
<p> Operating profit			  1,557 vs  1,657</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CHARGE   454 vs    182 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					     444 vs    577</p>
<p> Income after tax			    659 vs    898</p>
<p> Minorities			     CREDIT 1 vs	4 CHARGE</p>
<p> Net income				    660 vs    894</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll found analysts expected SKF to post a half year profit after financial items of 1.13 billion crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
